complex: Complex numbers

complex64 and complex128 are gp::complex64 and gp::complex128: two floats, the real part
first, as in Go. gocpp does not use std::complex, because its * and / follow C's Annex G and
differ between C++ libraries. Each operation is what gc does on amd64: the product is always
computed in float64 and never fused (-ffp-contract=off), and the quotient is Go's
runtime.complex128div, so (Inf+0i) * 2 is (+Inf+NaNi) as in Go, and a division by zero gives
infinities or NaN and never panics.

complex(r, i), real(c) and imag(c) are gp::complex128(r, i), gp::real(c) and gp::imag(c).
fmt prints a complex number as Go does, (1.5-2i).

Specification: docs/spec/cpp-mapping.md#complex-numbers
See also: gocpp explain types, gocpp explain fmt
Also known as: complex-numbers, complex numbers, complex128

Example (complex.gp):

    package main

    import "fmt"

    func main() {
    	c := complex(1.5, -2)
    	d := c * c
    	fmt.Println(d, real(d), imag(c) < 0)
    }

The C++ that gocpp emit -annotate writes for it:

    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #pragma once
    #include <gocpp/rt.hpp>

    namespace gpkg_main {
    void main();

    } // namespace gpkg_main
    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/complex.gp.cpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/complex.gp.cpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #include "gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp"

    namespace gpkg_main {

    // ---- ./complex.gp:5: func main() {
    void main() {

    // ---- ./complex.gp:6: c := complex(1.5, -2)
        gp::complex128 c = gp::complex128(1.5, -2.0);

    // ---- ./complex.gp:7: d := c * c
        gp::complex128 d = c * c;

    // ---- ./complex.gp:8: fmt.Println(d, real(d), imag(c) < 0)
    // gp[interfaces] col 2: fmt.Println: the runtime's gp::fmt functions take each operand with the
    //     descriptor of its Go type (gp::fmt::as), not boxed into an interface first (an operand of a
    //     non-pointer type with an Error method is, see the allocation note)
        gp::fmt::Println(d, gp::real(d), gp::imag(c) < 0.0);

    // ---- ./complex.gp:9: }
    }

    } // namespace gpkg_main
